Finish in ONE turn, checkpoint per item; end only when the report is written or blocked.

## 1. Strike (failed last round; verify with pixels, not code reading)
User sees: strike line still thin, and struck text renders heavier than plain text. Drop the TextDecoration approach. Draw the strike yourself: an IBackgroundRenderer on a layer ABOVE text (e.g. KnownLayer.Selection or a custom layer after Text) that draws a line per struck segment using the visual line geometry (BackgroundGeometryBuilder or VisualLine positions), thickness max(1.5, 0.1 * font size) DIP, vertically at x-height/2 above baseline, colour = run foreground. Make sure struck text keeps the exact typeface/weight/style of its neighbours (plain stays Regular, bold stays Bold, italic stays Italic).
PROOF REQUIRED: render a fixture line `plain ~~strike~~ **~~bold strike~~** *~~italic strike~~*` to PNG via RenderTargetBitmap (see demos/ui-variants for the pattern) in --selftest or a `--render-strike <out.png>` flag; save to .coord/reports/T-007-strike.png; measure in the bitmap that the line is >= 2 px tall at scale 1 and that "strike" glyph stroke darkness matches "plain" within tolerance. Report the numbers.

## 2. Markers
Look.MarkdownMarker one more notch dimmer (about 15% less contrast than #7E8B9B against the background). Keep it in Look (will become a user setting later).

## 3. Word-like list indent
When the caret sits right after a list marker with no item text (`- `, `* `, `- [ ] `, `1. ` etc.), Tab indents the whole item one level (keep marker; numbered item restarts at `1.` at the new level) and Shift+Tab outdents (renumber to continue the parent level when possible). One undo step. Normal Tab/Shift+Tab behaviour elsewhere unchanged.

## 4. Standard chrome + app bars (temporary, replaces borderless for now)
- Standard Windows title bar and borders (resizable, minimize/maximize/close). Close button = HIDE to tray (like Esc), not quit. Quit stays in tray (and in the app bar menu).
- Always-on-top OFF by default; Pin toggle in the top bar sets Topmost. Persist pin state.
- Top app bar: New note, Delete note, Previous / Next note, Pin, and a "…" menu (Quit). Bottom bar: note `n / count`, save status (Saved / Saving / error), hotkey hint. Replace the fading indicator with the bottom bar count. Keep the drag strip working (it may sit under the top bar).
- Styled from Look; plain is fine (polish later). Hotkey show/hide, single instance, focus-on-show and <100 ms show-to-focus must still hold; persist window size/position.

